== Pose gradients

On a box against the sky, where the edge term is the whole derivative, edge sampling matches CD on two of its three pose parameters (z = #F("edge.box_z2", 2) and #F("edge.box_z3", 2)). On the third it is #F("edge.box_rel1", 1)% high (z = #F("edge.box_z1", 2)), in every run we have made; the test's gate, four standard errors plus 3% of the reference, passes, but we have not found the cause. The device's f32 edge term matches the CPU's f64 to #E("edge.dev_vs_cpu"). On the shaded arm over a floor, the edge and interior terms alone miss CD by z = #F("sec.no_sec_z1", 2), #F("sec.no_sec_z2", 2), #F("sec.no_sec_z3", 2). The secondary term, mostly the arm's shadow on the floor, is #F("sec.share1", 0)%, #F("sec.share2", 0)% and #F("sec.share3", 0)% of the three derivatives. With secondary edges the same check gives z = #F("sec.floor_z1", 2), #F("sec.floor_z2", 2), #F("sec.floor_z3", 2) at 64 seeds; at 256 seeds the check fails, because the secondary estimate is heavy-tailed (@sec:discussion).

== From pixels to CAD parameters <sec:brep>

The edge sampler's velocity is a projection of the material point's motion, so replacing the pose's velocity with a unit translation per axis yields $partial cal(L) \/ partial x_i$ for every mesh vertex. vcad's differentiable seam @pedersen2026vcad takes that cotangent on the nodes of a frozen tessellation and returns the derivative with respect to a CAD parameter in one reverse pass. The shared benchmark uses rose's left shoulder-pitch output plate, a 3 mm rounded plate with a 49 mm bearing bore and twelve bolt holes, with $theta$ the bore diameter. irys renders vcad's frozen tessellation unchanged (#V("brep.nodes") nodes, #V("brep.tris") triangles). This is the mesh whose connectivity the kernel holds fixed while it differentiates node positions. The render is against the sky at 160×128, under a fixed smooth image loss.

